{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WM6D4H8vu892x7sXiLHG1e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"schema_version\": \"2.0\",\n3\t  \"id\": \"NSC-038\",\n4\t  \"contract_revision\": 3,\n5\t  \"contract_disposition\": \"active\",\n6\t  \"title\": \"Isometric Tilemap Architectural Visual Layer\",\n7\t  \"reconciliation_key\": \"isometric-tilemap-visual-layer\",\n8\t  \"kind\": \"implementation\",\n9\t  \"type\": \"world-foundation\",\n10\t  \"execution_scope\": \"single_agent\",\n11\t  \"execution_reason\": \"One agent can introduce the isometric Tilemap foundation and its representative visual-to-gameplay alignment check as a focused change.\",\n12\t  \"decomposition_state\": \"concrete\",\n13\t  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Tilemap grid, renderer, and architectural-tile authoring form one bounded visual-layer responsibility distinct from SpriteRenderer prefab conversion and integrated continuity validation.\",\n14\t  \"parent\": \"NSC-026\",\n15\t  \"depends_on\": [\n16\t    \"NSC-024\"\n17\t  ],\n18\t  \"exclusive_resources\": [\n19\t    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n20\t    \"unity-scene:Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\n21\t    \"logical:isometric-architectural-tile-assets\"\n22\t  ],\n23\t  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n24\t    {\n25\t      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-001\",\n26\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n27\t      \"requirement\": \"Establish an isometric Tilemap visual layer for floors, walls, and repeatable architectural tiles without transferring collision, walkability, trigger, door-state, or pursuit ownership into the Tilemap.\"\n28\t    }\n29\t  ],\n30\t  \"completion_gates\": [\n31\t    {\n32\t      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-001\",\n33\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Unity Validation Agent role (Section 4)\",\n34\t      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation compares representative Tilemap floor and wall visuals in effective world space against separately authored gameplay geometry, including coordinate, scale/footprint, offset, and orientation, so visual-only or gameplay-only desynchronization is detected.\"\n35\t    }\n36\t  ],\n37\t  \"downstream_integration_obligations\": [],\n38\t  \"gdd_evidence\": [\n39\t    {\n40\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n41\t      \"requirement\": \"The primary environment visual layer uses Unity Isometric Tilemaps for floors, walls, and repeatable architectural tiles.\"\n42\t    },\n43\t    {\n44\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n45\t      \"requirement\": \"The gameplay layer remains separate from the visible isometric art layer.\"\n46\t    }\n47\t  ],\n48\t  \"basis\": \"direct_gdd\",\n49\t  \"source_scope\": \"required\",\n50\t  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n51\t  \"notes\": \"This scope establishes reusable architectural authoring only; it excludes the five named room layouts and encounter content. Gameplay geometry remains authoritative and independently defined; Tilemap visuals may align to that geometry but must never define collider, walkability, trigger, door-state, or pursuit transforms. Persistent reusable architectural Tile assets are owned by this task through logical:isometric-architectural-tile-assets; exact placeholder asset filenames and appearance remain implementation details. Human-approved testability seam: the production scene builder may expose a narrow non-saving test entry point that constructs the current in-memory scene while using a caller-supplied temporary AssetDatabase folder for persistent architectural Tile assets. The seam must not open or save Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, must preserve the normal production Build() behavior and canonical generated-asset location, and must not transfer gameplay ownership into the Tilemap. Tests using the seam must create and remove their temporary assets and leave the repository clean.\",\n52\t  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"not_applicable\",\n53\t  \"repository_evidence_at_bootstrap\": [],\n54\t  \"provenance\": {\n55\t    \"graph_delta_plan_id\": \"GDP-9ed2e9f5d29e19e8e03f6907b7ecdd4e4deac9b8cb465283df856a88a3cc0db8\",\n56\t    \"origin\": \"progressive_decomposition\",\n57\t    \"parent_contract_revision\": 1,\n58\t    \"parent_contract_sha256\": \"8dd459df6c99ef48df5ee4893db957150139abc7eedded1e8098799e9b115177\",\n59\t    \"parent_task_id\": \"NSC-026\"\n60\t  }\n61\t}\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fea62c35-9f6f-442a-af18-7c3971bc0dbc","uuid":"12cfc447-6c39-4932-9769-5bbd18d7a9be","timestamp":"2026-09-01T22:02:49.257Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/Tasks/NSC-038.yaml","content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"NSC-038\",\n  \"contract_revision\": 3,\n  \"contract_disposition\": \"active\",\n  \"title\": \"Isometric Tilemap Architectural Visual Layer\",\n  \"reconciliation_key\": \"isometric-tilemap-visual-layer\",\n  \"kind\": \"implementation\",\n  \"type\": \"world-foundation\",\n  \"execution_scope\": \"single_agent\",\n  \"execution_reason\": \"One agent can introduce the isometric Tilemap foundation and its representative visual-to-gameplay alignment check as a focused change.\",\n  \"decomposition_state\": \"concrete\",\n  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Tilemap grid, renderer, and architectural-tile authoring form one bounded visual-layer responsibility distinct from SpriteRenderer prefab conversion and integrated continuity validation.\",\n  \"parent\": \"NSC-026\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"NSC-024\"\n  ],\n  \"exclusive_resources\": [\n    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n    \"unity-scene:Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\n    \"logical:isometric-architectural-tile-assets\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Establish an isometric Tilemap visual layer for floors, walls, and repeatable architectural tiles without transferring collision, walkability, trigger, door-state, or pursuit ownership into the Tilemap.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"completion_gates\": [\n    {\n      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-001\",\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Unity Validation Agent role (Section 4)\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation compares representative Tilemap floor and wall visuals in effective world space against separately authored gameplay geometry, including coordinate, scale/footprint, offset, and orientation, so visual-only or gameplay-only desynchronization is detected.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"downstream_integration_obligations\": [],\n  \"gdd_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n      \"requirement\": \"The primary environment visual layer uses Unity Isometric Tilemaps for floors, walls, and repeatable architectural tiles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n      \"requirement\": \"The gameplay layer remains separate from the visible isometric art layer.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"basis\": \"direct_gdd\",\n  \"source_scope\": \"required\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"This scope establishes reusable architectural authoring only; it excludes the five named room layouts and encounter content. Gameplay geometry remains authoritative and independently defined; Tilemap visuals may align to that geometry but must never define collider, walkability, trigger, door-state, or pursuit transforms. Persistent reusable architectural Tile assets are owned by this task through logical:isometric-architectural-tile-assets; exact placeholder asset filenames and appearance remain implementation details. Human-approved testability seam: the production scene builder may expose a narrow non-saving test entry point that constructs the current in-memory scene while using a caller-supplied temporary AssetDatabase folder for persistent architectural Tile assets. The seam must not open or save Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, must preserve the normal production Build() behavior and canonical generated-asset location, and must not transfer gameplay ownership into the Tilemap. Tests using the seam must create and remove their temporary assets and leave the repository clean.\",\n  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"not_applicable\",\n  \"repository_evidence_at_bootstrap\": [],\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"graph_delta_plan_id\": \"GDP-9ed2e9f5d29e19e8e03f6907b7ecdd4e4deac9b8cb465283df856a88a3cc0db8\",\n    \"origin\": \"progressive_decomposition\",\n    \"parent_contract_revision\": 1,\n    \"parent_contract_sha256\": \"8dd459df6c99ef48df5ee4893db957150139abc7eedded1e8098799e9b115177\",\n    \"parent_task_id\": \"NSC-026\"\n  }\n}\n","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018rVjtbhn6UAi8ntFkSBrDy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"schema_version\": \"2.0\",\n3\t  \"id\": \"NSC-039\",\n4\t  \"contract_revision\": 1,\n5\t  \"contract_disposition\": \"active\",\n6\t  \"title\": \"World-Space SpriteRenderer Prefab and Sorting Foundation\",\n7\t  \"reconciliation_key\": \"world-sprite-prefab-sorting\",\n8\t  \"kind\": \"implementation\",\n9\t  \"type\": \"world-foundation\",\n10\t  \"execution_scope\": \"single_agent\",\n11\t  \"execution_reason\": \"After the Tilemap baseline exists, one agent can establish the SpriteRenderer prefab convention, apply it to representative prototype objects, and validate their sorting behavior.\",\n12\t  \"decomposition_state\": \"concrete\",\n13\t  \"decomposition_reason\": \"World-space prefab representation and its shared isometric sorting convention are a cohesive responsibility separate from Tilemap architecture and simulation-layer continuity.\",\n14\t  \"parent\": \"NSC-026\",\n15\t  \"depends_on\": [\n16\t    \"NSC-038\"\n17\t  ],\n18\t  \"exclusive_resources\": [\n19\t    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n20\t    \"unity-scene:Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\n21\t  ],\n22\t  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n23\t    {\n24\t      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-001\",\n25\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n26\t      \"requirement\": \"Establish reusable world-space SpriteRenderer prefab and sorting conventions for the wizard, enemies, doors, props, obstacles, and other independently sorted or interactive objects, keeping those objects outside the architectural Tilemap.\"\n27\t    }\n28\t  ],\n29\t  \"completion_gates\": [\n30\t    {\n31\t      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-001\",\n32\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Unity Validation Agent role (Section 4)\",\n33\t      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation exercises representative world-space SpriteRenderers at different isometric positions and confirms their ordering relative to Tilemap geometry and to one another follows the established isometric sorting convention.\"\n34\t    }\n35\t  ],\n36\t  \"downstream_integration_obligations\": [],\n37\t  \"gdd_evidence\": [\n38\t    {\n39\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n40\t      \"requirement\": \"The wizard, enemies, taller props, interactive doors, obstacles, decorative set pieces, and other independently sorted objects use world-space SpriteRenderers and prefabs rather than being painted into a Tilemap.\"\n41\t    },\n42\t    {\n43\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Required feedback and character presentation\",\n44\t      \"requirement\": \"The wizard and enemies follow the same isometric sorting conventions as other world-space SpriteRenderers; placeholder character sprites are acceptable.\"\n45\t    }\n46\t  ],\n47\t  \"basis\": \"direct_gdd\",\n48\t  \"source_scope\": \"required\",\n49\t  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n50\t  \"notes\": \"This proposed scope defines the reusable representation and sorting convention; it does not author enemy behavior, room-specific props, or final visual assets.\",\n51\t  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"not_applicable\",\n52\t  \"repository_evidence_at_bootstrap\": [],\n53\t  \"provenance\": {\n54\t    \"graph_delta_plan_id\": \"GDP-9ed2e9f5d29e19e8e03f6907b7ecdd4e4deac9b8cb465283df856a88a3cc0db8\",\n55\t    \"origin\": \"progressive_decomposition\",\n56\t    \"parent_contract_revision\": 1,\n57\t    \"parent_contract_sha256\": \"8dd459df6c99ef48df5ee4893db957150139abc7eedded1e8098799e9b115177\",\n58\t    \"parent_task_id\": \"NSC-026\"\n59\t  }\n60\t}\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fea62c35-9f6f-442a-af18-7c3971bc0dbc","uuid":"c509a67f-c887-416d-a6c9-530308a3980a","timestamp":"2026-09-01T22:02:49.259Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/Tasks/NSC-039.yaml","content":"{\n  \"sc