{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BND67pEFeUSwo2fdqnf6QN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"schema_version\": \"2.0\",\n3\t  \"id\": \"NSC-042\",\n4\t  \"contract_revision\": 1,\n5\t  \"contract_disposition\": \"active\",\n6\t  \"title\": \"Seamless Scalable Wall Tiling for Long Isometric Walls\",\n7\t  \"reconciliation_key\": \"seamless-scalable-wall-tiling\",\n8\t  \"kind\": \"implementation\",\n9\t  \"type\": \"world-foundation\",\n10\t  \"execution_scope\": \"single_agent\",\n11\t  \"execution_reason\": \"One agent can refine the wall visual authoring convention established by NSC-039 so independently sortable wall cells repeat cleanly across short and very long walls without changing simulation ownership.\",\n12\t  \"decomposition_state\": \"concrete\",\n13\t  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Human runtime validation isolated a specific follow-up: one-cell wall segmentation fixes sorting, but the current placeholder wall artwork visibly restarts at segment boundaries and needs a reusable seamless tiling convention that scales to long walls.\",\n14\t  \"parent\": \"NSC-026\",\n15\t  \"depends_on\": [\n16\t    \"NSC-039\"\n17\t  ],\n18\t  \"exclusive_resources\": [\n19\t    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n20\t    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\",\n21\t    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Generated/ArchitecturalTiles/WallTile.asset\",\n22\t    \"unity-scene:Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\n23\t  ],\n24\t  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n25\t    {\n26\t      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-001\",\n27\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction; human runtime observation during NSC-039 validation\",\n28\t      \"requirement\": \"Provide a reusable one-cell wall visual convention whose repeated tiles join without visible gaps, border seams, or pattern-phase resets that make each sorting segment read as a separate piece of wall at normal gameplay camera distance.\"\n29\t    },\n30\t    {\n31\t      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-002\",\n32\t      \"reference\": \"NSC-039 - World-Space SpriteRenderer Prefab and Sorting Foundation\",\n33\t      \"requirement\": \"Preserve independently sortable wall cells and the positional isometric sorting behavior established by NSC-039; do not solve visual continuity by returning to one monolithic renderer for a long wall, by forcing the player to a fixed higher Order in Layer, or by otherwise bypassing positional sorting.\"\n34\t    },\n35\t    {\n36\t      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-003\",\n37\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n38\t      \"requirement\": \"Scale straight-wall authoring by repeating a bounded reusable wall-tile asset set so a wall of approximately 100 cells does not require 100 uniquely authored Sprite or Tile assets and does not require a unique full-length wall image.\"\n39\t    },\n40\t    {\n41\t      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-004\",\n42\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n43\t      \"requirement\": \"Keep wall presentation independent from gameplay collision and simulation ownership so visual segmentation, tiling, or placeholder-art changes do not redefine the wall's gameplay collider topology or behavior.\"\n44\t    }\n45\t  ],\n46\t  \"completion_gates\": [\n47\t    {\n48\t      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-001\",\n49\t      \"reference\": \"Unity Validation Agent role; human runtime observation\",\n50\t      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation constructs representative straight walls of at least 3, 10, and 100 visual cells and confirms they use the reusable wall visual convention continuously without gaps or asset-count growth proportional to wall length.\"\n51\t    },\n52\t    {\n53\t      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-002\",\n54\t      \"reference\": \"NSC-039 - VAL-001\",\n55\t      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation confirms the wizard can move along both sides of and cross a representative long wall while front/behind ordering remains correct under the NSC-039 sorting convention.\"\n56\t    },\n57\t    {\n58\t      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-003\",\n59\t      \"reference\": \"Human runtime observation\",\n60\t      \"requirement\": \"Human validation at the normal gameplay camera confirms the repeated straight wall reads as one continuous wall rather than a row of visibly restarting wall pieces.\"\n61\t    }\n62\t  ],\n63\t  \"downstream_integration_obligations\": [],\n64\t  \"gdd_evidence\": [\n65\t    {\n66\t      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n67\t      \"requirement\": \"Architectural presentation is authored in the isometric visual layer while gameplay collision and other simulation behavior remain separately owned.\"\n68\t    }\n69\t  ],\n70\t  \"basis\": \"direct_gdd\",\n71\t  \"source_scope\": \"required\",\n72\t  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n73\t  \"notes\": \"This is an explicit follow-up to NSC-039 and must not block closing NSC-039 once its sorting foundation is conformant. Scope is straight-wall visual continuity and scalable repetition. Final wall art, decorative variation, corners, junctions, end caps, and room-specific wall dressing are out of scope unless a minimal treatment is required to prove seamless straight-wall repetition.\",\n74\t  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"not_applicable\",\n75\t  \"repository_evidence_at_bootstrap\": [],\n76\t  \"provenance\": {\n77\t    \"origin\": \"human_scope_correction\",\n78\t    \"source_task_id\": \"NSC-039\",\n79\t    \"source_task_revision_before_move\": 1,\n80\t    \"reason\": \"Human runtime validation confirmed NSC-039's one-cell wall segmentation fixes player/wall sorting, but exposed a separate visual-quality and scalability concern: repeated placeholder wall segments do not join cleanly and future walls may span roughly 100 cells. The issue was deliberately deferred so NSC-039 can finish without expanding its scope.\"\n81\t  }\n82\t}\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fea62c35-9f6f-442a-af18-7c3971bc0dbc","uuid":"220551c1-4808-4f23-856f-aaa00a5b5750","timestamp":"2026-09-01T22:03:12.257Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/Tasks/NSC-042.yaml","content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"NSC-042\",\n  \"contract_revision\": 1,\n  \"contract_disposition\": \"active\",\n  \"title\": \"Seamless Scalable Wall Tiling for Long Isometric Walls\",\n  \"reconciliation_key\": \"seamless-scalable-wall-tiling\",\n  \"kind\": \"implementation\",\n  \"type\": \"world-foundation\",\n  \"execution_scope\": \"single_agent\",\n  \"execution_reason\": \"One agent can refine the wall visual authoring convention established by NSC-039 so independently sortable wall cells repeat cleanly across short and very long walls without changing simulation ownership.\",\n  \"decomposition_state\": \"concrete\",\n  \"decomposition_reason\": \"Human runtime validation isolated a specific follow-up: one-cell wall segmentation fixes sorting, but the current placeholder wall artwork visibly restarts at segment boundaries and needs a reusable seamless tiling convention that scales to long walls.\",\n  \"parent\": \"NSC-026\",\n  \"depends_on\": [\n    \"NSC-039\"\n  ],\n  \"exclusive_resources\": [\n    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\",\n    \"repo-file:Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Generated/ArchitecturalTiles/WallTile.asset\",\n    \"unity-scene:Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-001\",\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction; human runtime observation during NSC-039 validation\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Provide a reusable one-cell wall visual convention whose repeated tiles join without visible gaps, border seams, or pattern-phase resets that make each sorting segment read as a separate piece of wall at normal gameplay camera distance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-002\",\n      \"reference\": \"NSC-039 - World-Space SpriteRenderer Prefab and Sorting Foundation\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Preserve independently sortable wall cells and the positional isometric sorting behavior established by NSC-039; do not solve visual continuity by returning to one monolithic renderer for a long wall, by forcing the player to a fixed higher Order in Layer, or by otherwise bypassing positional sorting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-003\",\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Scale straight-wall authoring by repeating a bounded reusable wall-tile asset set so a wall of approximately 100 cells does not require 100 uniquely authored Sprite or Tile assets and does not require a unique full-length wall image.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-004\",\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Keep wall presentation independent from gameplay collision and simulation ownership so visual segmentation, tiling, or placeholder-art changes do not redefine the wall's gameplay collider topology or behavior.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"completion_gates\": [\n    {\n      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-001\",\n      \"reference\": \"Unity Validation Agent role; human runtime observation\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation constructs representative straight walls of at least 3, 10, and 100 visual cells and confirms they use the reusable wall visual convention continuously without gaps or asset-count growth proportional to wall length.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-002\",\n      \"reference\": \"NSC-039 - VAL-001\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Unity validation confirms the wizard can move along both sides of and cross a representative long wall while front/behind ordering remains correct under the NSC-039 sorting convention.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-003\",\n      \"reference\": \"Human runtime observation\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Human validation at the normal gameplay camera confirms the repeated straight wall reads as one continuous wall rather than a row of visibly restarting wall pieces.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"downstream_integration_obligations\": [],\n  \"gdd_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD - Environment Presentation and Authoring Direction\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Architectural presentation is authored in the isometric visual layer while gameplay collision and other simulation behavior remain separately owned.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"basis\": \"direct_gdd\",\n  \"source_scope\": \"required\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"This is an explicit follow-up to NSC-039 and must not block closing NSC-039 once its sorting foundation is conformant. Scope is straight-wall visual continuity and scalable repetition. Final wall art, decorative variation, corners, junctions, end caps, and room-specific wall dressing are out of scope unless a minimal treatment is required to prove seamless straight-wall repetition.\",\n  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"not_applicable\",\n  \"repository_evidence_at_bootstrap\": [],\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"origin\": \"human_scope_correction\",\n    \"source_task_id\": \"NSC-039\",\n    \"source_task_revision_before_move\": 1,\n    \"reason\": \"Human runtime validation confirmed NSC-039's one-cell wall segmentation fixes player/wall sorting, but exposed a separate visual-quality and scalability concern: repeated placeholder wall segments do not join cleanly and future walls may span roughly 100 cells. The issue was deliberately deferred so NSC-039 can finish without expanding its scope.\"\n  }\n}\n","numLines":83,"startLine":1,"tota